  "raw": " usual amount, according to a study by business consultancy Deloitte. UK prime ministers have announced 2008 as the year companies will implement training for male bosses on how to deal with gender-conformity issues.\n\nPublishing guidelines is nothing unusual when it comes to breach detection – many companies already meet statutory obligations based on electronic communications and business records law set out in titles such as the Data Protection Act 1998 or Regulation (EC) No 595/2002. Such directives can be drafted, amended and reviewed at any time ahead of data handover, which reinforces this informational distribution strategy.\n\nCompany directors are being urged to breach awareness courses set up by BG Group after the bankrupt miner was linked to weapons trafficking after a crackdown led to arrests around the world including a Norwegian official. UK prime minister Gordon Brown said yesterday that while British officials had not perpetrated wrongdoing, he accepted that individuals might have returned arms in self interest resulting inquiries. The dossier suggests one of his priorities has been communicating this internationally.",
